 Primitive Age

 Purpose

The Primitive Age is the transition between vanilla survival and industrialization.

The player begins working with basic industrial materials and primitive processing systems while preparing the infrastructure required for the Steam Age.

The Primitive Age should gradually move the player away from purely vanilla progression without immediately introducing advanced automation or power systems.

 Resources

Define the resources required for the Primitive Age.

* Copper
* Tin
* Zinc
* Iron
* Coal
* Redstone
* Other required materials

 Tools

Define the tools available during the Primitive Age.

Primitive tools should improve upon basic vanilla infrastructure without providing access to higher-tier industrial equipment.

 Processing

Define how raw resources are processed during the Primitive Age.

Processing should remain relatively manual or limited in automation.

The Primitive Age should establish the basic material-processing chains required for the Steam Age.

 Machines

Define the first machines available during the Primitive Age.

Machines should provide basic processing capabilities while remaining significantly below Steam-tier automation.

 Automation

Automation should be limited during the Primitive Age.

The player should still perform a significant amount of processing manually and build the infrastructure necessary for future automation.

 Requirements

Define the requirements for entering the Primitive Age.

The player should first establish a stable vanilla foundation before beginning Primitive progression.

 Exit Condition

The Primitive Age ends when the player has acquired the materials, infrastructure, and knowledge required to begin the Steam Age.

The final objective of the Primitive Age is to prepare the player for the first Steam-powered industrial systems.
